Third-party dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GaleQEA is licensed under Apache-2.0. Every bundled runtime dependency is
permissively licensed (MIT / BSD / Apache-2.0 / ISC / MPL-2.0 / PSF and similar),
with one reviewed exception:

  * psycopg / psycopg-binary (LGPL-3.0-only). The PostgreSQL driver ships only in
    the optional `postgres` extra, is dynamically imported, and is user-replaceable;
    its weak copyleft does not propagate to GaleQEA. A SQLite install bundles no
    LGPL code at all.

AGPL / BSL / SSPL components (e.g. MinIO, Redis 8, Grafana) are never bundled: they
are only ever documented, self-hosted integrations that an operator opts into.

Any future non-permissive dependency must be added as a named, rationalised
exception in `.github/scripts/check_licenses.py`; the CI license gate fails on an
undocumented one.
